From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:08:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 071/207] In-model runner: answer fences after reasoning,
 compile-and-run shells, no inline prior

Live re-smoke code cells owned 0/8:
- the think block's end has no bytes, so an answer opening with a fence was read mid-line and every later fence paired one off; the boundary now ends the line
- a shell fence that only compiles or runs (gcc x.c -o x && ./x) no longer takes the header from the program cell before it
- inline cells are no longer passed as notebook state, which made the frontend refuse every later code cell
